  <item>
    <title>Virginia (data center power tax): data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/virginia-data-center-power-tax-va</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-virginia-(data-center-power-tax)-va</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>2026-28 budget keeps the data center sales-and-use tax exemption but adds the first statewide electricity consumption tax on data centers — $0.011/kWh from Jul 1, capped at $600M a year with the excess refunded. Not a moratorium, and not a zoning restriction</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Virginia Beach: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/virginia-beach-va</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-virginia-beach-va</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>12-month pause on new data center applications, 10-0, ending early if the council adopts a data center ordinance first. Aimed at larger-scale and hyperscale proposals; does not affect the existing Globalinx facility. Staff told the council the city has no established definitions, setbacks or noise thresholds yet. Reported as a Tuesday vote in coverage published before Aug 20; Aug 18 is that Tuesday</description>
  </item>
